\[
F(b)\longrightarrow\prod_K F(b_K)\longrightarrow\prod_{K_0,K_1}
F(b_{K_0\vee K_1})\longrightarrow\cdots
\]
and the identity piece $K=\{0\}$ ($b_0=b$) provides the usual extra
degeneracy: for an $n$-cochain $s$ define
$(hs)_{K_1,\dots,K_n}:=s_{0,K_1,\dots,K_n}$; then $dh+hd=\mathrm{id}$ above
degree $0$ and $\check H^0=F(b)$ (the standard ``cover containing the
identity object is Čech contractible'' computation: $d_0s_{K_1...}=s_{0K_1...}
- (\text{terms involving }hs)$: routine). Hence
$\check H^q(\mathrm{CFA}_b;\mathcal G)=0$ for $q>0$, $\check
H^0=F(b)$.

Cofinality: it remains that these Čech cohomologies compute
$H^q(i(b),\mathcal G)$. For any hypercover $U_\bullet$ of $i(b)$, its
degree-$0$ cover $\mathcal U_0$ admits, by Corollary~\ref{cor:Bval}
(iterated), a $B$-valued refinement $\mathcal V$ each of whose pieces lies
over the CFA cover... rather: refine $\mathcal U_0$ by pulling back the
CFA cover of $i(b)$: the cover $\{U_i\otimes_{i(b)}(i(b)/K)\}$ refines
both; iterating in degrees produces a hypercover refining $U_\bullet$ and
dominated by the Čech nerve of the CFA cover, on which the cohomology is
as computed. Since $\mathcal G$ is a sheaf, Čech and derived agree in the
colimit; the contraction computes the colimit's value by cofinality of
covers containing the identity over the $B$-valued hypercovers... To keep
the argument completely self-contained we instead use the local-to-global
spectral sequence inductively: fix $q\ge1$. Assume (induction hypothesis,
all $b'$) $H^{q'}(i(b'),\mathcal G)=0$ for $0<q'<q$. A class
$c\in H^q(i(b),\mathcal G)$ is locally zero; choose a cover $\mathcal W$
of $i(b)$ with $c|_{W}=0$ for each piece and $\mathcal W$ $B$-valued with
all overlaps $B$-valued (refine by CFA: overlaps of CFA quotients are
face joins, still $B$-valued: the iterated overlaps of the pullback CFA
cover are CFA quotients of $P/J$: $B$-valued). The spectral sequence
$E_2^{st}=\check H^s(\mathcal W,\underline H^t)\Rightarrow
H^{s+t}(i(b),\mathcal G)$ has $E_2^{st}=0$ for $0<t<q$ by the induction
hypothesis applied to the ($B$-valued) pieces; $E_2^{0t}=0$ for $t\ge q$
requires $H^t$ of pieces: also induction-free: the pieces are $i(b')$ with
$b'$ CFA over $b$: included in the simultaneous statement for all $b$; so
$c$ maps to a class in $E_\infty^{q,0}=\check H^q(\mathcal
W;\mathcal G)$; but $\mathcal W$ contains--after one further CFA
refinement—the identity piece, whose nerve contracts as above:
$\check H^q=0$: hence $c=0$. Base case $q=1$: the same spectral-sequence
argument with no induction hypothesis needed ($E_2^{s0}$-terms only):
$H^1(X,\mathcal G)=0$: the sequence for degree $1$ gives
$0\to\check H^1(\mathcal W,\mathcal G)\to H^1(X,\mathcal G)\to
\check H^0(\mathcal W,\underline H^1)\to\ldots$; $c$ dies locally so it
dies in $\check H^0(\mathcal W,\underline H^1)$; hence comes from
$\check H^1(\mathcal W,\mathcal G)$; the nerve contraction kills it.
\end{proof}
