$i(b)$. There is a standard rigid refinement $R^\flat$ of $R$ and a
refinement map of families $\sigma:S\to R^\flat$ such that
every non-refusal \textup{(}kernel-$J$\textup{)} piece of $S$ occurs
literally as an $R^\flat$-piece and $\sigma$ is the identity
there.
\end{lemma}
